From: Weaver development toolchain
Subject: [PATCH] internal/fuzz: recognize the parent deadline before child cancellation

Backport of upstream Go commit 5a957dc766aed011cdfe7c953987a2ff86c0829c.
https://go.googlesource.com/go/+/5a957dc766aed011cdfe7c953987a2ff86c0829c
The parent error is stored before Done closes, but the child error may lag.
This changes neither the fuzz duration nor handling of non-context failures.

--- a/src/internal/fuzz/fuzz.go
+++ b/src/internal/fuzz/fuzz.go
@@ -129,3 +129,3 @@
-		if err == fuzzCtx.Err() || isInterruptError(err) {
+		if err == ctx.Err() || err == fuzzCtx.Err() || isInterruptError(err) {
 			// Suppress cancellation errors and terminations due to SIGINT.
 			// The messages are not helpful since either the user triggered the error
